===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|coughen}}, {{m|enm|coghen|t=to cough; to vomit}}{{nb...|coghe, couhen, couwhen, couwe, couwen, couȝen, couȝhen, couȝtthe, couȝwen, coȝen, cowen, cowff, cowghen, cowhen, cowȝen, koghe, kouȝen, kowen|otherforms=1}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*cohhian}} (compare {{cog|ang|cohhetan|t=to bluster; to riot; to cough (?)}}), from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*kuh-|t=to cough}}, ultimately of {{glossary|onomatopoeic}} origin.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=1058916649|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

